{"key":"m03/a-banner-printer","id":"a-banner-printer","title":"A banner printer","kind":"project","level":3,"minutes":90,"check":"io","tags":[],"lesson":null,"milestone":{"id":"m03","title":"Everything Is Numbers","color":"#edbc5c","index":3},"description":"Lesson 3.02 showed that a font is just numbers. Use one to print text in big letters.\n\nThe starter holds a tiny font: every character is **3 pixels wide and 5 tall**, and each row is a number whose 3 bits are its pixels (the bit worth 4 on the left, 1 on the right). `'A': [2, 5, 7, 5, 5]` is:\n\n```\n.#.    2 = 010\n#.#    5 = 101\n###    7 = 111\n#.#    5 = 101\n#.#    5 = 101\n```\n\nRead one line and print it as a banner: 5 lines of text, `#` for a pixel that is on and a space for one that is off, with **one blank column between characters**. Lower-case letters are printed as upper case, and any character not in the font is printed as `?`. Trailing spaces at the ends of lines do not matter.\n\nFor the input `HI` the program prints (after the prompt `Text? `):\n\n```\n# # ###\n# #  #\n###  #\n# #  #\n# # ###\n```","starter":{"main.py":"FONT = {\n    'A': [2, 5, 7, 5, 5], 'B': [6, 5, 6, 5, 6], 'C': [3, 4, 4, 4, 3], 'D': [6, 5, 5, 5, 6],\n    'E': [7, 4, 6, 4, 7], 'F': [7, 4, 6, 4, 4], 'G': [3, 4, 5, 5, 3], 'H': [5, 5, 7, 5, 5],\n    'I': [7, 2, 2, 2, 7], 'J': [1, 1, 1, 5, 2], 'K': [5, 5, 6, 5, 5], 'L': [4, 4, 4, 4, 7],\n    'M': [5, 7, 7, 5, 5], 'N': [6, 5, 5, 5, 5], 'O': [2, 5, 5, 5, 2], 'P': [6, 5, 6, 4, 4],\n    'Q': [2, 5, 5, 6, 3], 'R': [6, 5, 6, 5, 5], 'S': [3, 4, 2, 1, 6], 'T': [7, 2, 2, 2, 2],\n    'U': [5, 5, 5, 5, 7], 'V': [5, 5, 5, 5, 2], 'W': [5, 5, 7, 7, 5], 'X': [5, 5, 2, 5, 5],\n    'Y': [5, 5, 2, 2, 2], 'Z': [7, 1, 2, 4, 7], '0': [7, 5, 5, 5, 7], '1': [2, 6, 2, 2, 7],\n    '2': [6, 1, 2, 4, 7], '3': [6, 1, 2, 1, 6], '4': [5, 5, 7, 1, 1], '5': [7, 4, 6, 1, 6],\n    '6': [3, 4, 7, 5, 7], '7': [7, 1, 2, 2, 2], '8': [7, 5, 7, 5, 7], '9': [7, 5, 7, 1, 6],\n    ' ': [0, 0, 0, 0, 0], '?': [6, 1, 2, 0, 2], '!': [2, 2, 2, 0, 2],\n}\ntext = input(\"Text? \")\nprint(text)\n"},"solution":{"main.py":"FONT = {\n    'A': [2, 5, 7, 5, 5], 'B': [6, 5, 6, 5, 6], 'C': [3, 4, 4, 4, 3], 'D': [6, 5, 5, 5, 6],\n    'E': [7, 4, 6, 4, 7], 'F': [7, 4, 6, 4, 4], 'G': [3, 4, 5, 5, 3], 'H': [5, 5, 7, 5, 5],\n    'I': [7, 2, 2, 2, 7], 'J': [1, 1, 1, 5, 2], 'K': [5, 5, 6, 5, 5], 'L': [4, 4, 4, 4, 7],\n    'M': [5, 7, 7, 5, 5], 'N': [6, 5, 5, 5, 5], 'O': [2, 5, 5, 5, 2], 'P': [6, 5, 6, 4, 4],\n    'Q': [2, 5, 5, 6, 3], 'R': [6, 5, 6, 5, 5], 'S': [3, 4, 2, 1, 6], 'T': [7, 2, 2, 2, 2],\n    'U': [5, 5, 5, 5, 7], 'V': [5, 5, 5, 5, 2], 'W': [5, 5, 7, 7, 5], 'X': [5, 5, 2, 5, 5],\n    'Y': [5, 5, 2, 2, 2], 'Z': [7, 1, 2, 4, 7], '0': [7, 5, 5, 5, 7], '1': [2, 6, 2, 2, 7],\n    '2': [6, 1, 2, 4, 7], '3': [6, 1, 2, 1, 6], '4': [5, 5, 7, 1, 1], '5': [7, 4, 6, 1, 6],\n    '6': [3, 4, 7, 5, 7], '7': [7, 1, 2, 2, 2], '8': [7, 5, 7, 5, 7], '9': [7, 5, 7, 1, 6],\n    ' ': [0, 0, 0, 0, 0], '?': [6, 1, 2, 0, 2], '!': [2, 2, 2, 0, 2],\n}\n\ndef row_text(bits):\n    return \"\".join(\"#\" if (bits >> k) & 1 else \" \" for k in (2, 1, 0))\n\ndef glyph(ch):\n    ch = ch.upper()\n    return FONT[ch] if ch in FONT else FONT[\"?\"]\n\ntext = input(\"Text? \")[:20]\nfor row in range(5):\n    print(\" \".join(row_text(glyph(ch)[row]) for ch in text).rstrip())\n"},"entry":"main.py","match":"exact","hints":["For one character, row `r` of the banner is `row_text(FONT[ch][r])`. For the whole line, join every character's row with a single space."],"requirements":["Use the font's numbers: test each bit with `>>` and `&`, do not type out the letters as pictures.","Write a function `row_text(bits)` that turns one 3-bit row into 3 characters, and use it for every character.","Stop at 20 characters of input; ignore the rest."],"stretch":"","rules":["Read the pixels from the font's numbers with `>>` and `&`."],"examples":[{"name":"hi","stdin":"HI\n","expected":"Text? # # ###\n# #  #\n###  #\n# #  #\n# # ###"},{"name":"lower case and digits","stdin":"code 2026\n","expected":"Text?  ##  #  ##  ###     ##  ### ##   ##\n#   # # # # #         # # #   # #\n#   # # # # ##       #  # #  #  ###\n#   # # # # #       #   # # #   # #\n ##  #  ##  ###     ### ### ### ###"}],"unitTests":"","lang":"python","testCount":4,"lessonTitle":null,"prev":null,"next":null,"grading":{"key":"m03/a-banner-printer","kind":"project","level":3,"check":"io","match":"exact","entry":"main.py","timeout":4000,"strict":false,"lang":"python","rules":[{"type":"must","pattern":">>|&","message":"Read the pixels from the font's numbers with `>>` and `&`."}],"unitTests":"","support":{},"tests":[{"name":"hi","stdin":"HI\n","args":[],"expected":"Text? # # ###\n# #  #\n###  #\n# #  #\n# # ###"},{"name":"lower case and digits","stdin":"code 2026\n","args":[],"expected":"Text?  ##  #  ##  ###     ##  ### ##   ##\n#   # # # # #         # # #   # #\n#   # # # # ##       #  # #  #  ###\n#   # # # # #       #   # # #   # #\n ##  #  ##  ###     ### ### ### ###"},{"name":"the whole alphabet","stdin":"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRST\n","args":[],"expected":"Text?  #  ##   ## ##  ### ###  ## # # ###   # # # #   # # ##   #  ##   #  ##   ## ###\n# # # # #   # # #   #   #   # #  #    # # # #   ### # # # # # # # # # # #    #\n### ##  #   # # ##  ##  # # ###  #    # ##  #   ### # # # # ##  # # ##   #   #\n# # # # #   # # #   #   # # # #  #  # # # # #   # # # # # # #   ##  # #   #  #\n# # ##   ## ##  ### #    ## # # ###  #  # # ### # # # #  #  #    ## # # ##   #"},{"name":"the rest and unknown characters","stdin":"UVWXYZ 0123456789 #!?\n","args":[],"expected":"Text? # # # # # # # # # # ###     ###  #  ##  ##  # # ###  ## ### ### ###     ##   #\n# # # # # # # # # #   #     # # ##    #   # # # #   #     # # # # #       #  #\n# # # # ###  #   #   #      # #  #   #   #  ### ##  ###  #  ### ###      #   #\n# # # # ### # #  #  #       # #  #  #     #   #   # # #  #  # #   #\n###  #  # # # #  #  ###     ### ### ### ##    # ##  ###  #  ### ##       #   #"}]}}